<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<!-- Remote push (bridge revision 9). `development` routes a debug build to
	     sandbox APNs; App Store / TestFlight signing rewrites this to
	     `production` automatically. Both APNs keys live in both Firebase
	     projects (docs/building.md, "Push credentials"), so either environment
	     can deliver regardless of which backend the build talks to.

	     Still deliberately absent: com.apple.developer.associated-domains
	     (M2 adds it for Universal Links).

	     Wanted, and waiting on Apple: com.apple.developer.networking.multicast.
	     "Expose Minecraft server to your local network" turns on Pumpkin's LAN
	     broadcast (a datagram to 224.0.2.60:4445 every 1.5 s, which is how a
	     Java client's Multiplayer screen lists a server on the Wi-Fi), and iOS
	     refuses multicast sends without this entitlement — Pumpkin binds its
	     socket and every send fails quietly. It is requested through the form
	     at developer.apple.com/contact/request/networking-multicast, on the
	     developer account, with a human review. Until it is granted the
	     toggle exposes the server but does not list it, and the doc says so.
	     Once granted, add
	       <key>com.apple.developer.networking.multicast</key><true/>
	     here and to the App ID's capabilities; nothing in the code changes. -->
	<key>aps-environment</key>
	<string>development</string>
</dict>
</plist>
